WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.920
Hey Youtubers it's Charlie! Huge news for Legend Of Korra tonight.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.000
So they're airing all 4 final episodes tonight. Janet Varney made the announcement on

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:17.630
Tumblr.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.800
They said that if they could get 10,000
reblogs they would air the final two

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:21.390
episodes

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.810
a week early on Nick.com at midnight
tonight. This video will be a review of

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:28.890
episodes 11 and 12, and then I'll do a
separate review for episode 13 and 14.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.050
Be sure to SUBSCRIBE to get it. Since
there's so much awesome Korra to get

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.360
through tonight, let's do our favorite
moments real quick

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.750
and then I'll do my review. First off,
high five yourself if you guessed

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.500
Dark Avatar.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.559
Unalaq explained that once Harmonic Convergence started he would fuse with Vaatu.

00:00:42.559 --> 00:00:45.210
And because they would be in perfect
alignment they would be a much more

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.390
powerful Avatar

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:50.260
than Raava and Korra would be. This
doesn't explain how he can be the Avatar

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.859
without having all four elements.

00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:55.559
But I think that the show runners just
want to imply that Vaatu would give him

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:59.190
that ability just like Raava kind of held
all four element for Wan.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.109
But that doesn't confirm whether or not
there will actually be a Dark Avatar.

00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:04.230
We'll find out in those last two episodes
though.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.690
So we got to see Harmonic Convergence and
the visual effect as well as the

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.770
soundtrack during a lot of the scenes
was amazing.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.850
Watching that wave of dark energy just
envelope the entire planet.

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:17.380
If you're confused about what that means, it
means when Harmonic Convergence happens it

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.630
basically amplifies spiritual energy so

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:23.079
any spirits walking around now are 10
times more powerful. It doesn't explain

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:26.299
whether all benders become more powerful,
but spirits definitely become more

00:01:26.299 --> 00:01:26.729
powerful.

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:30.020
That's why Vaatu is able to break out
of his tree prison. That classic Fire

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:33.590
Ferrets scene at the end was also amazing
obviously Bolin kind of had his moment

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.259
the beginning of the episode in the arena.

00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:38.469
Bolin and Mako were basically running a
block on Unalaq while Korra was trying to

00:01:38.469 --> 00:01:38.899
close the portal.

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:42.170
She didn't do it in time, but it was still
amazing seeing Classic Fire Ferrets.

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.259
Fire Ferrets Ride or Die!

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:47.369
Next up, my two favorite characters in
these two episodes were

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:50.920
1 - Bolin, or should I say Nuktuk, Sky Warrior.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.500
And 2- Bumi with his flute. The last couple
episodes Bolin's characters kind of got

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:58.880
pushed to the side while Korra deals with
her spiritual mis alignment or tries to

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.240
get realigned with Raava.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.799
So was awesome to watch him get his big
hero moment in the arena. Especially

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:04.369
when the

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:07.380
action on-screen started a mirror the
action in the arena.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.479
I actually thought that the Bolin and Asami were going to hook up in that first episode,

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:13.860
but it turns out Masami is still a
thing. But I'll talk about that during my

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.000
funniest moments.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.180
So Bumi was my favorite character from
Harmonic Convergence.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.800
Not only did he inception Team Korra with
the aerial assault idea,

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:25.190
he also took out the entire southern
encampment guarding the portal.

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:28.520
Obviously it was a funny scene too,
but we learned that you can pacify

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.870
spirits with music.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.620
So obviously not all spirits, because that
led to that big destruction scene.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.730
But I think that his flute is going to come in
handy later or its going inform some of

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:37.900
the character's strategy.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.360
Raise your hand if you that the
soundtrack during that whole Bumi

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.810
destruction seen when he climbed in the
Mech was amazing!

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.930
The sound just picked up and was perfect
for that scene. It was

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.190
hilarious and the action was amazing.
As a side note, I'll also probably be doing a

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.800
giveaway for the Korra soundtrack
whenever they release the Book 2

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.550
soundtrack.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:57.060
As for my funniest scenes in the episodes
though, even though Bumi kind of brought

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:57.910
most of the comedy,

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:01.250
the Masami VS Makorra specially
in that first episode

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:05.670
was amazing. Write below in the comments, "How many different expressions do you think

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.300
went across Mako's face

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.880
when he tried to deal with Korra and
Asami. It must have been at least 20.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.530
20 expressions of awkward in under 30 seconds,

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.070
it was hilarious. Poor Mako... He brought
this on himself though.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:21.210
But the big questions we had after this
episode and before the Finale are

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:25.660
1 - Will Unalaq fuse with Vaatu and how 
wil Korra stop them if they do become the

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:28.940
Dark Avatar? Remember they're supposed to
be more powerful than she and Raava

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:29.450
together.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.150
2 - How will they save Jinora? We didn't see Jinora in this episode, but she's still

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.480
in the spirit world. 3 - Will the twins
betray Unalaq and help Team Korra?

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.920
and 4 - What will Korra do to pacify all
the dark spirits roaming around in the

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:42.590
human realm?

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:46.530
Even if she does defeat Unalaq and
Vaatu and closes the spirit portals.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.960
That won't make the spirits go away. So
she'll still have to pacify them

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:53.070
and get them to go back through the
Spirit Portal into the Spirit World.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:56.090
But what did I think of the episode? Overall 
I give it a solid B+

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.110
It was great. I really loved the way it
took side characters

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:02.330
or at least main characters that hadn't
been serviced and really gave them big

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.530
moments. It paid off a lot of moments for
people like Bolin and Bumi.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:08.870
They had kind of been pushed to the side for a long time. The action was great, the

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.780
soundtrack was great. It's still not as
good as Beginnings. Beginnings is still

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.820
my all-time favorite Korra episode right
now.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.120
But it went a long way to answering some of
our biggest questions like the Dark

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.220
Avatar question.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.389
Even though there are a bunch of questions that still remain unanswered, we'll find out

00:04:22.389 --> 00:04:23.169
after the Finale.

00:04:23.169 --> 00:04:25.789
Because it literally, the last two
episodes will be airing at Midnight

00:04:25.789 --> 00:04:26.419
tonight

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:29.979
on Nick.com. That's Eastern Time. I'll be doing a video for that

00:04:29.979 --> 00:04:32.919
Be sure to SUBSCRIBE to get it. I'll post it
right after the episode airs so will be

00:04:32.919 --> 00:04:33.699
late tonight.

00:04:33.699 --> 00:04:35.979
But let me know your favorite moments were
and if there was anything that you

00:04:35.979 --> 00:04:38.830
thought was really important that I didn't
mention in the video, it was an hour

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.870
Korra so there's a lot of stuff that went on.
Be sure to write in the comments and

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:42.830
we'll discussify.

